From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: SourbyCraft <dev@iyanz.dev>
Date: Tue, 19 May 2026 00:00:00 +0700
Subject: [PATCH] feat(v6): enable virtual threads for Minecraft server thread pools

When SourbyCraftConfig.virtualThreads is true, all server internal
thread pools (BACKGROUND_EXECUTOR, IO_POOL, DIMENSION_DATA_IO_POOL,
DOWNLOAD_POOL) use Executors.newVirtualThreadPerTaskExecutor() instead
of ForkJoinPool / CachedThreadPool / FixedThreadPool.

Virtual threads are lightweight (~1KB stack) and enable unbounded
concurrency without platform thread overhead.

diff --git a/src/main/java/net/minecraft/util/Util.java b/src/main/java/net/minecraft/util/Util.java
index 1e77bcc..b590a29 100644
--- a/src/main/java/net/minecraft/util/Util.java
+++ b/src/main/java/net/minecraft/util/Util.java
@@ -83,6 +83,7 @@ import net.minecraft.SharedConstants;
 import net.minecraft.SuppressForbidden;
